---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SEO, SITE } from '../config/site';
const updated = '2026';
---
<BaseLayout title={SEO.privacy.title} description={SEO.privacy.description}>
  <PageHead title="Privacy policy" lead="How we handle the details you give us, under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018." crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy policy' }]} />

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose-fk">
        <p class="t-small">Last updated {updated}.</p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>{SITE.name} is a mobile HGV locksmith and diagnostics business based in {SITE.baseTown}, {SITE.baseRegion}. We are the controller of the personal data described here. You can reach us on <a href={`tel:${SITE.phoneTel}`}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a> by phone or WhatsApp.</p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Details you send through our forms, by phone or on WhatsApp: your name, phone number, email if you give it, the lorry (make, model, year, registration), where it is and what you need.</li>
          <li>Proof of ownership we check before key or module work: we look at your V5C and photo ID, or an operator’s letter of authorisation. We may note the document type and the details needed to show the check was done.</li>
          <li>Payment and invoice records for work we carry out.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why we use it and our lawful basis</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To reply to your enquiry, quote and carry out the job: steps taken at your request before and under a contract.</li>
          <li>To check that a vehicle belongs to the person asking for keys: our legitimate interest in preventing vehicle crime, and protecting you.</li>
          <li>To keep invoices and accounts: our legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not use your details for marketing and we do not sell them.</p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Formspree</strong>, which delivers website form submissions to us by email.</li>
          <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> (Meta), if you choose to message us there.</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong>, if you view the map on our contact page. The map loads from Google and Google may set cookies when you use it.</li>
          <li>Our website host, which keeps short-term server logs (such as IP addresses) to run and protect the site.</li>
          <li>Our accountant, HMRC or the police where the law requires it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Some of these providers may process data outside the UK. Where they do, they rely on safeguards recognised under UK law.</p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>Enquiries that do not lead to a job are deleted within 12 months. Job and invoice records are kept for six years for tax purposes, then deleted.</p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>This website does not use analytics or advertising cookies. We store one setting in your browser to remember that you have hidden the cookie notice. The Google map on the contact page may set its own cookies when it loads.</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, object to how we use it or ask us to restrict it. Call or message us on {SITE.phoneDisplay}. We reply within one month.</p>
        <p>If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123 1113.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
